{"id": 8, "timestamp": "2025-12-19T20:52:53.715357", "source": "agent", "message": "I read the file /app/stp/README.markdown.", "cause": 7, "observation": "read", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "str_replace_editor", "tool_call_id": "toolu_02", "model_response": {"id": "msg_vrtx_01XEx63bidVWKGZEBWtYfBcs", "created": 1766177573, "model": "claude-sonnet-4", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "Let me check the README to understand the build instructions for STP:", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"command\": \"view\", \"path\": \"/app/stp/README.markdown\"}", "name": "str_replace_editor"}, "id": "toolu_02", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 54, "prompt_tokens": 6354, "total_tokens": 6408, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 6351}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "content": "Here's the result of running `cat -n` on /app/stp/README.markdown:\n     1\t[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)\n     2\t[![Linux build](https://travis-ci.org/stp/stp.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/stp/stp)\n     3\t[![Windows build](https://ci.appveyor.com/api/projects/status/35983b7cnrg37whk?svg=true)](https://ci.appveyor.com/project/msoos/stp)\n     4\t[![Documentation](https://readthedocs.org/projects/stp/badge/?version=latest)](https://stp.readthedocs.io/en/latest/?badge=latest)\n     5\t[![Coverity](https://scan.coverity.com/projects/861/badge.svg)](https://scan.coverity.com/projects/861)\n     6\t[![Codacy Badge](https://api.codacy.com/project/badge/Grade/f043efa22ea64e9ba44fde0f3a4fb09f)](https://www.codacy.com/app/soos.mate/cryptominisat?utm_source=github.com&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=msoos/cryptominisat&amp;utm_campaign=Badge_Grade)\n     7\t[![Coverage](https://coveralls.io/repos/stp/stp/badge.svg?branch=master&service=github)](https://coveralls.io/github/stp/stp?branch=master)\n     8\t\n     9\t# STP\n    10\t\n    11\tSTP is a constraint solver (or SMT solver) aimed at solving constraints of bitvectors and arrays. These types of constraints can be generated by program analysis  tools, theorem provers, automated bug finders, cryptographic attack tools, intelligent fuzzers, model checkers, and by many other applications.\n    12\t\n    13\t* Homepage:      https://stp.github.io/\n    14\t* Ubuntu PPA:    https://launchpad.net/~simple-theorem-prover/+archive/ubuntu/ppa/+packages\n    15\t* Docker image:  `docker pull msoos/stp`\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\t## Build and install\n    19\t\n    20\tFor a quick install:\n    21\t\n    22\t```\n    23\tsudo apt-get install cmake bison flex libboost-all-dev python perl minisat\n    24\tgit clone https://github.com/stp/stp\n    25\tcd stp\n    26\tmkdir build\n    27\tcd build\n    28\tcmake ..\n    29\tmake\n    30\tsudo make install\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\tFor more detailed instructions, see towards the end of the page.\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t## Input format\n    37\t\n    38\tThe file based input formats that STP reads are the: CVC, SMT-LIB1, and SMT-LIB2 formats. The SMT-LIB2 format is the recommended file format, because it is parsed by all modern bitvector solvers. Only quantifier-free bitvectors and arrays are implemented from the SMTLibv2 format.\n    39\t\n    40\t### Usage\n    41\t\n    42\tRun with an SMTLibv2 file:\n    43\t```\n    44\tstp myproblem.smt\n    45\t```\n    46\t\n    47\tOverflowing a 32b integer using the python interface:\n    48\t```\n    49\timport stp\n    50\tIn [1]: import stp\n    51\tIn [2]: a = stp.Solver()\n    52\tIn [3]: x = a.bitvec('x')\n    53\tIn [4]: y = a.bitvec('y')\n    54\tIn [5]: a.add(x + y < 20)\n    55\tIn [6]: a.add(x  > 10)\n    56\tIn [7]: a.add(y  > 10)\n    57\tIn [8]: a.check()\n    58\tOut[8]: True\n    59\tIn [9]: a.model()\n    60\tOut[9]: {'x': 4294967287L, 'y': 11L}\n    61\t```\n    62\t\n    63\tWith Docker:\n    64\t```\n    65\tdocker pull msoos/stp\n    66\techo \"(set-logic QF_BV)\n    67\t(assert (= (bvsdiv (_ bv3 2) (_ bv2 2)) (_ bv0 2)))\n    68\t(check-sat)\n    69\t(exit)\" | docker run --rm -i msoos/stp\n    70\t```\n    71\t\n    72\t## Architecture\n    73\t\n    74\tThe system performs word-level preprocessing followed by translation to SAT which is then solved by a SAT solver. In particular, we introduce several new heuristics for the preprocessing step, including abstraction-refinement in the context of arrays, a new bitvector linear arithmetic equation solver, and some interesting simplifications. These heuristics help us achieve several magnitudes of order performance over other tools, and also over straight-forward translation to SAT. STP has been heavily tested on thousands of examples sourced from various real-world applications such as program analysis and bug-finding tools like EXE, and equivalence checking tools and theorem-provers.\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t## Detailed Building and Installation\n    78\t\n    79\tSTP is built with [CMake](https://cmake.org/), version 3.0.2 or newer. CMake is a\n    80\tmeta build system that generates build files for other tools such as\n    81\tmake(1), Visual Studio, Xcode, etc.\n    82\t\n    83\t### Configuration variables\n    84\tHere are a few interesting configuration variables. These apply to all\n    85\tgenerators.\n    86\t\n    87\t- ``CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`` - The build type (e.g. Release)\n    88\t- ``CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`` - The prefix for install (e.g. /usr/local )\n    89\t- ``ENABLE_ASSERTIONS`` - If TRUE STP will be built with asserts.\n    90\t- ``ENABLE_TESTING`` - Enable running tests\n    91\t- ``ENABLE_PYTHON_INTERFACE`` - Enable building the Python interface\n    92\t- ``PYTHON_EXECUTABLE`` - Set python executable in case you have more than one python installed\n    93\t- ``SANITIZE`` - Use Clang's sanitization checks\n    94\t- ``STATICCOMPILE`` - Build static libraries and binaries instead of dynamic\n    95\t\n    96\t### Dependencies\n    97\tSTP relies on : boost, flex, bison and minisat. You can install these by:\n    98\t\n    99\t```\n   100\t$ sudo apt-get install cmake bison flex libboost-all-dev python perl minisat\n   101\t```\n   102\t\n   103\tSTP uses minisat as its SAT solver by default but it also supports other SAT solvers including CryptoMiniSat as an optional extra. If installed, it will be detected during the cmake and used:\n   104\t\n   105\t```\n   106\t$ git clone https://github.com/msoos/cryptominisat\n   107\t$ cd cryptominisat\n   108\t$ mkdir build && cd build\n   109\t$ cmake ..\n   110\t$ make\n   111\t$ sudo make install\n   112\t$ sudo ldconfig\n   113\t```\n   114\t\n   115\t### Building a static library and binary\n   116\t\n   117\t```\n   118\t$ mkdir build && cd build\n   119\t$ cmake -DSTATICCOMPILE=ON ..\n   120\t$ make\n   121\t$ sudo make install\n   122\t$ sudo ldconfig```\n   123\t```\n   124\t\n   125\t### Configuration and build options\n   126\t\n   127\tTo tweak the build configuration:\n   128\t\n   129\t* Run ``cmake-gui /path/to/stp/source/root`` instead of ``cmake``. This\n   130\t  user interface lets you control the value of various configuration\n   131\t  variables and lets you pick the build system generator.\n   132\t\n   133\t* Run ``ccmake`` instead of ``cmake``. This provides an ncurses terminal\n   134\t  interface for changing configuration variables.\n   135\t\n   136\t* Pass ``-D<VARIABLE>=<VALUE>`` options to ``cmake`` (not very user friendly).\n   137\t  It is probably best if you **only** configure this way if you are writing\n   138\t  scripts.\n   139\t\n   140\tYou can also tweak configuration later by running `make edit_cache` and edit any configuration variables, reconfigure and then regenerate the build system. After configuration, build by running `make`.\n   141\t\n   142\tYou can use the `-j<n>` flag to significantly to decrease build time by running `<n>` jobs in parallel (e.g. `make -j4`).\n   143\t\n   144\t### Testing\n   145\t\n   146\t```\n   147\tgit clone https://github.com/stp/stp\n   148\tgit submodule update --init\n   149\tpip install lit\n   150\tmkdir build\n   151\tcd build\n   152\tcmake -DENABLE_TESTING=ON ..\n   153\tmake\n   154\tmake check\n   155\t```\n   156\t\n   157\t### Installing\n   158\t\n   159\tTo install run `make install` and to uninstall run `make uninstall`. The root of installation is controlled by the `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX` variable at configure time. You can change this by running `make edit_cache` and editing the value of `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX`.\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t### Building on Visual Studio\n   163\t\n   164\tLet's assume you put STP's source into c:\\projects\\stp and you have cygwin and\n   165\tgit installed. Get zlib:\n   166\t\n   167\t```\n   168\tcd C:\\projects\n   169\tgit clone https://github.com/madler/zlib\n   170\tcd zlib\n   171\tgit checkout v1.2.8\n   172\tmkdir build\n   173\tmkdir myinstall\n   174\tcd build\n   175\tcmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\"..\\myinstall\" ..\n   176\tcmake --build .\n   177\tcmake --build . --target install\n   178\t```\n   179\t\n   180\tGet minisat:\n   181\t\n   182\t```\n   183\tcd C:\\projects\n   184\tgit clone https://github.com/stp/minisat\n   185\tcd minisat\n   186\tmkdir build\n   187\tmkdir myinstall\n   188\tcd build\n   189\tcmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=\"..\\myinstall\" -DZLIB_ROOT=\"..\\..\\zlib\\myinstall\" ..\n   190\tcmake --build .\n   191\tcmake --build . --target install\n   192\t```\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\tGet flex, bison, perl:\n   196\t\n   197\t```\n   198\tC:\\cygwin64\\setup-x86_64.exe  -qnNd -R C:/cygwin64 -s http://cygwin.mirror.constant.com -l C:/cygwin64/var/cache/setup --packages \"flex,bison,perl\"\n   199\t```\n   200\t\n   201\tFinally, Build STP:\n   202\t\n   203\t```\n   204\tcd C:\\projects\n   205\tgit clone https://github.com/stp/stp\n   206\tgit submodule update --init --recursive\n   207\tmkdir build\n   208\tcd build\n   209\tcmake -DBoost_USE_STATIC_LIBS=ON -DENABLE_TESTING=ON -DPYTHON_EXECUTABLE=\"C:\\Program Files\\Python36\\\\python.exe\" -DLIT_TOOL=\"C:\\Program Files\\Python36\\Scripts\\\\lit.exe\" -DMINISAT_LIBDIR=\"..\\..\\minisat\\myinstall\\lib\" -DMINISAT_INCLUDE_DIRS=\"..\\..\\minisat\\myinstall\\include\" -DZLIB_ROOT=\"..\\..\\zlib\\myinstall\" -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=\"C:\\cygwin64\" ..\n   210\tcmake --build .\n   211\tcmake --build . --target install\n   212\t```\n   213\t\n   214\t### Building Docker\n   215\t\n   216\t```\n   217\tgit clone https://github.com/stp/stp\n   218\tcd stp\n   219\tdocker build -t stp .\n   220\techo \"(set-logic QF_BV)\n   221\t(assert (= (bvsdiv (_ bv3 2) (_ bv2 2)) (_ bv0 2)))\n   222\t(check-sat)\n   223\t(exit)\" | docker run --rm -i stp\n   224\t```\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\t# Authors\n   228\t\n   229\t* Vijay Ganesh\n   230\t* Trevor Hansen\n   231\t* Mate Soos\n   232\t* Dan Liew\n   233\t* Ryan Govostes\n   234\t* And many others...\n   235\t\n   236\t\n", "extras": {"path": "/app/stp/README.markdown", "impl_source": "oh_aci"}}
