{"id": 65, "timestamp": "2025-12-19T20:59:36.661541", "source": "agent", "message": "All done! What's next on the agenda?", "action": "finish", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "finish", "tool_call_id": "toolu_31", "model_response": {"id": "msg_vrtx_0168YUwpYj697cepG6jz3VhR", "created": 1766177976, "model": "claude-sonnet-4", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"message\": \"Task completed successfully! I have successfully built and installed the Simple Theorem Prover (STP) from /app/stp. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\\n\\n## Installation Summary:\\n\\n1. **Dependencies installed**: cmake, bison, flex, zlib1g-dev, minisat\\n2. **Fixed compilation issue**: Added missing `#include <cstdint>` to `/app/stp/include/stp/AST/ASTNode.h`\\n3. **Built STP**: Successfully compiled with make after resolving the header issue\\n4. **Installed STP**: Installed to `/usr/local/bin/stp_simple` and created symlink as `/usr/local/bin/stp`\\n5. **Configured library paths**: Updated ldconfig to ensure shared libraries are found\\n\\n## Verification:\\n\\nThe `stp` command is now available as a shell command and working correctly:\\n- \\u2705 Can be executed from any directory: `stp` command is available in PATH\\n- \\u2705 Successfully processes SMT-LIB2 input format\\n- \\u2705 Can solve satisfiability problems and return models\\n- \\u2705 Handles both satisfiable and unsatisfiable cases correctly\\n\\n## Example Usage:\\n```bash\\necho \\\"(set-logic QF_BV)(declare-fun x () (_ BitVec 32))(assert (= x (_ bv42 32)))(check-sat)(exit)\\\" | stp\\n```\\n\\nSTP is now ready to use for constraint solving, bitvector operations, and array reasoning tasks.\", \"task_completed\": \"true\"}", "name": "finish"}, "id": "toolu_31", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 386, "prompt_tokens": 60948, "total_tokens": 61334, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 60945}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "llm_metrics": {"accumulated_cost": 0.0, "max_budget_per_task": null, "accumulated_token_usage": {"model": "default", "prompt_tokens": 1242213, "completion_tokens": 2504, "cache_read_tokens": 396411, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "context_window": 0, "per_turn_token": 61334, "response_id": ""}, "costs": [], "response_latencies": [], "token_usages": []}, "args": {"final_thought": "Task completed successfully! I have successfully built and installed the Simple Theorem Prover (STP) from /app/stp. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Installation Summary:\n\n1. **Dependencies installed**: cmake, bison, flex, zlib1g-dev, minisat\n2. **Fixed compilation issue**: Added missing `#include <cstdint>` to `/app/stp/include/stp/AST/ASTNode.h`\n3. **Built STP**: Successfully compiled with make after resolving the header issue\n4. **Installed STP**: Installed to `/usr/local/bin/stp_simple` and created symlink as `/usr/local/bin/stp`\n5. **Configured library paths**: Updated ldconfig to ensure shared libraries are found\n\n## Verification:\n\nThe `stp` command is now available as a shell command and working correctly:\n- ✅ Can be executed from any directory: `stp` command is available in PATH\n- ✅ Successfully processes SMT-LIB2 input format\n- ✅ Can solve satisfiability problems and return models\n- ✅ Handles both satisfiable and unsatisfiable cases correctly\n\n## Example Usage:\n```bash\necho \"(set-logic QF_BV)(declare-fun x () (_ BitVec 32))(assert (= x (_ bv42 32)))(check-sat)(exit)\" | stp\n```\n\nSTP is now ready to use for constraint solving, bitvector operations, and array reasoning tasks.", "task_completed": "true", "outputs": {}, "thought": ""}}
